97.\n\nSo all bytes should be initialized. Unless there's a case where `x == 1` (single pixel width)?\n\nIf `x == 1`, then the loop at line 4578:\n```c\nfor (i=x-1; i >= 1; --i, ...)\n```\nbecomes:\n```c\nfor (i=0; i >= 1; --i, ...)\n```\nThis loop doesn't execute at all! So for a 1-pixel-wide image, only pixel 0 is processed by the first-byte handling code. The alpha for pixel 0 is set at lines 4543-4545. So this should be fine.\n\nLet me think about another scenario. What if `depth == 16` and `img_n == out_n`? Then the code takes the `if (depth < 8 || img_n == out_n)` branch at line 4557. In this case:\n- `nk = (width - 1) * filter_bytes`\n- The loop processes `nk` bytes starting from `cur` (which already points past pixel 0)\n\nFor `img_n == out_n`, there's no alpha channel to add, so `filter_bytes == output_bytes`. The loop processes all remaining bytes in the row. This should be fine.\n\nOK, let me try a different approach. Let me look at the actual reproducer testcase from OSS-Fuzz:", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"index": 1, "function": {"arguments": "{\"url\": \"https://oss-fuzz.com/download?testcase_id=6193806570684416\"}", "name": "web_read"}, "id": "toolu_26", "type": "function"}], "function_call": null}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1966, "prompt_tokens": 30473, "total_tokens": 32439, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 29056}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 29056, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 1417}}, "total_calls_in_response": 1}, "content": "\n", "extras": {"url": "about:blank", "trigger_by_action": "browse", "screenshot": "data:image/png;base64,", "set_of_marks": "data:image/png;base64,", "error": true, "goal_image_urls": [], "open_pages_urls": ["about:blank"], "active_page_index": 0, "dom_object": {"documents": [{"documentURL": 0, "title": -1, "baseURL": 0, "contentLanguage": -1, "encodingName": 1, "publicId": -1, "systemId": -1, "frameId": 2, "nodes": {"parentIndex": [-1, 0, 1, 1]